# command-site — Site Changer Mode

> **Invoke:** Type `command-site` or `@command-site` to enter this mode. Manual only — never auto-applied.

---

## What This Mode Does

When the user invokes **command-site**, the agent enters **site changer mode**:

1. **Scope:** Only website-related files and repo items. Central platform work is off-limits.
2. **Styling:** All edits follow `STYLE-GUIDE.md` and the relevant `.mdc` rules in `.cursor/rules/` (website + general-formatting rules — see `README.md` index).
3. **Boundary:** Do not read, edit, or reference Central-related files or MDC rules.

---

## In-Scope (Website Only)

| Area | Paths / Files |
|------|---------------|
| **Pages** | `Pages/`, `index.html`, `index-*.html`, `dev-index.html` |
| **Components** | `Components/` |
| **Templates** | `Templates/` |
| **Styles** | `css/`, `*.css` in Components/Templates |
| **Scripts** | `js/`, `scripts/` (build, scaffold — carousel, etc.) |
| **Media** | `media/` |
| **Content** | `Create/`, `email-templates/`, `prompts-main/` |
| **Docs** | `STYLE-GUIDE.md`, `LAYOUT-STANDARDS.md`, `SEO-GUIDELINES.md`, `ASSETS-REFERENCE.md`, `JS-PATTERNS.md` |
| **Website rules** | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (see `README.md` — website & marketing + general formatting) |

---

## Out-of-Scope (Do Not Touch)

| Area | Paths / Files |
|------|---------------|
| **Central** | `Dev/central/` (all of it) |
| **Central rules** | Any `.mdc` that applies to Central (RLS, CRM, dashboard, migrations, etc.) |
| **Applications** | `Applications/` (deployable apps with backend) |

**Rule:** If a file lives under `Dev/central/` or is a Central-scoped rule, do not read or edit it in site changer mode.

---

## Styling Authority (When Editing)

In site changer mode, apply these in order:

1. **`STYLE-GUIDE.md`** — CSS variables, typography, navigation, hero, sections, CTAs, spacing.
2. **Website & marketing `.mdc`** — `cta-formatting.mdc`, `header-subheader-centering.mdc`, `dynamic-image-carousel.mdc`, `Creative-Mode.mdc` (when doing copy).
3. **General formatting `.mdc`** — `typography.mdc`, `spacing.mdc`, `color.mdc`, `elevation.mdc`, `shape.mdc`, `motion.mdc`, `layout.mdc`, `accessibility.mdc`.

---

## Pre-Flight (Site Changer Mode)

Before editing any website file:

- **Scope check:** Is this file under `Dev/central/` or Central-related? If yes → stop. Not in scope.
- **Style check:** Does this change affect layout, typography, or components? If yes → read `STYLE-GUIDE.md` and relevant website MDC first.
- **Carousel check:** If touching carousel HTML/images → use source-of-truth workflow (`pickleball-carousel-source-of-truth.mdc`).

